From ddbfbd8a2ca2f65258876f5b5b9f2c40d393669d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Axis Build Agent <agent@regentplatform.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 11:39:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Fix the actual cause of the popup deadlock: stale Radix
 versions + version conflict, plus a global failsafe
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause found: package.json pinned every @radix-ui/react-* package to
versions from late 2024 (react-dialog ^1.1.2, react-dropdown-menu ^2.1.1,
etc.), and the lockfile had a duplicate @radix-ui/react-dialog@1.0.5 pulled
in transitively alongside 1.1.2. This exact combination — stale version +
duplicate sub-dependency versions of @radix-ui/react-dismissable-layer —
is the documented cause of Radix's long-running 'pointer-events: none
stuck on body' bug (radix-ui/primitives#1241, #3317, #3445, #3645), which
upstream has fixed and partially regressed across several releases. Our
own useDeferredModalOpen workaround (already applied to InvoiceActions,
JournalEntryActions) reduces the race window but doesn't fix a genuinely
broken dependency tree.

Fix:
- Bumped all 27 @radix-ui/react-* packages in package.json to their
  current published versions (react-dialog 1.1.2 -> 1.1.23, etc.)
- Clean node_modules + package-lock.json reinstall — confirmed only one
  version of @radix-ui/react-dialog now resolves in the tree (was two)
- Added RadixPointerEventsFailsafe (mounted once in app/layout.tsx): a
  global belt-and-suspenders net that clears a stuck
   whenever no Radix overlay is actually
  present in the DOM. Runs on a short delay after every click (when the
  dropdown->dialog transition that triggers this actually happens) plus a
  low-frequency interval sweep. Never touches pointer-events while a real
  modal/dropdown/popover is legitimately open.

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit passes clean, npm ls shows no UNMET/invalid
peer deps, no duplicate @radix-ui/react-dialog versions in package-lock.json.
